  "title": "Adani Ports ESG Disclosures: Labour, Ethics, Risk, Supply Chain",
  "summary": "This page from Adani Ports' 2024-25 Integrated Annual Report covers four ESG sections: Labour Relations Management (GRI 3-3, 402; KPIs on complaints and engagement sessions; risks of noncompliance, penalties, strikes; opportunities for productivity and stakeholder value; governance and mitigation via compliance and communication); Business Ethics (GRI 3-3, 205; KPIs on conflict of interest, corruption, misconduct complaints and anti-bribery training; risks of penalties, reputation damage, capital challenges; opportunities for transparency via maker-checker; mitigation through Code of Conduct, training, whistleblower and POSH mechanisms, data privacy); Risk Management (GRI 3-3, 2-24; KPIs on ERM committee meetings and site coverage; risks from market, regulatory, cyber, process failures; opportunities for resilience and trust; mitigation via ERM committee and Board oversight); and Supply Chain Management (GRI 3-3, 204, 308, 414; KPIs on ESG supplier screening and corrective actions; opportunities for sustainability, risk mitigation, ethical practices, and reputation enhancement).",
}
